{"slug":"first-unique-character","title":"First Unique Character","topic":"arrays-strings","difficulty":"easy","order":117,"tags":["strings","counting","frequency"],"timeLimitMs":2000,"concept":{"title":"Counting letters in a table of 26","body":["For lowercase letters you can count how often each letter occurs with a table of 26 numbers: the letter `c` has the index `ord(c) - ord(\"a\")`. One pass fills the table.",{"code":"count = [0] * 26\nfor ch in s:\n    count[ord(ch) - ord(\"a\")] += 1"},"A second pass can then ask the table about each character. Two passes with a small table beat comparing every character with every other one."]},"statement":["Given a word of lowercase English letters, find the first character that appears exactly once in the word. Print its index (counting from 0), or -1 if there is no such character."],"inputFormat":["A single word `s`."],"outputFormat":["Print one integer."],"constraints":["1 <= length of s <= 20000"],"examples":[{"input":"leetcode\n","output":"0\n","note":"l appears once and is at index 0."},{"input":"aabb\n","output":"-1\n","note":"Every letter repeats."}],"hints":["Count how often each letter appears.","Use an array of 26 counters and `ord(ch) - ord(\"a\")` as the index.","Then scan the word from the left and stop at the first letter whose counter is 1."],"starter":{"python":"s = input().strip()\n\n# Your code here\n","cpp":"#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <string>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint main() {\n    string s;\n    cin >> s;\n\n    // Your code here\n\n    return 0;\n}\n","java":"import java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        String s = sc.next();\n\n        // Your code here\n    }\n}\n"},"solution":{"explanation":["The first pass counts the letters. The second pass returns the first position whose letter has a count of 1."],"complexity":"Time O(n), space O(1) (26 counters).","code":{"python":"s = input().strip()\n\ncount = [0] * 26\nfor ch in s:\n    count[ord(ch) - ord(\"a\")] += 1\nanswer = -1\nfor i, ch in enumerate(s):\n    if count[ord(ch) - ord(\"a\")] == 1:\n        answer = i\n        break\nprint(answer)\n","cpp":"#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <string>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint main() {\n    string s;\n    cin >> s;\n\n    int count[26] = {0};\n    for (char ch : s) count[ch - 'a']++;\n    int answer = -1;\n    for (int i = 0; i < (int) s.size(); i++) {\n        if (count[s[i] - 'a'] == 1) {\n            answer = i;\n            break;\n        }\n    }\n    cout << answer << \"\\n\";\n\n    return 0;\n}\n","java":"import java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        String s = sc.next();\n\n        int[] count = new int[26];\n        for (int i = 0; i < s.length(); i++) count[s.charAt(i) - 'a']++;\n        int answer = -1;\n        for (int i = 0; i < s.length(); i++) {\n            if (count[s.charAt(i) - 'a'] == 1) {\n                answer = i;\n                break;\n            }\n        }\n        System.out.println(answer);\n    }\n}\n"}},"tests":[{"input":"leetcode\n","output":"0\n"},{"input":"aabb\n","output":"-1\n"},{"input":"z\n","output":"0\n"},{"input":"aab\n","output":"2\n"},{"input":"abab\n","output":"-1\n"},{"input":"loveleetcode\n","output":"2\n"},{"input":"befbdfffdbdffdabadacdeeaaccfad\n","output":"-1\n"},{"input":"\n","output":"-1\n"},{"input":"abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzabcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzabcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzabcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzabcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzabcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzxabcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzabcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzabcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz\n","output":"-1\n"},{"input":"\n","output":"-1\n"}]}